well the go true blue campaign it's  underway celebrating both national law  enforcement day and the 50th anniversary  of the Las Vegas Metropolitan Police  Department Mary Jane ballessa shares how  the city and Clark County are  celebrating  take a look behind me where a number of  strip resorts are lighting up their  iconic Marquees in blue to express their  support for the Las Vegas Metropolitan  Police Department police captain Gregory  Munson recalls working at Metro 25 years  ago so I have the 25th anniversary badge  and then now here I stand here today  with the 50th Anniversary badge 25 years  later and uh and part of a great  organization Clark County Commissioners  and Community Partnerships showed their  support Monday afternoon at the welcome  to Las Vegas sign Tom Kovac is the  executive director of the Las Vegas  Metropolitan Police Department  Foundation we at the foundation uh you  know just are doing our part in trying  to raise the funds to make their jobs  even better and to help the public  understand how amazing amazing and  heroic they often can be even when no  one is watching locals like Mary rendina  say volunteering through Metro is also a  great way to get involved in the  community rendina's husband did so in  the past if you're just willing to help  they have people that are volunteering  from age 30 to age 80. you know with  some of the jobs that they do whether  they're desk jobs or helping events to  take tickets they just do so so much in  the community that some of it gets  recognized and some of it they're kind  of our unsung heroes Munson says it's  Community relationships like these that  make our city that much stronger there's  a lot of things that impact our  community poverty and people that are  starving people that are unhoused and it  takes the business Community it takes  our private Partners it takes the police  department the County Commissioners all  as one to come together to solve these  problems  Metro as we know it today was created in  1973 when the city of Las Vegas Police  in Clark County Sheriff's Department  combined into one force
 

